{"strongs": "H8184", "word": "שְׂעֹרָה", "translit": "se.o.rah", "root": "שער", "morph": "H:N-F", "pos": "noun feminine", "gloss": "barley", "definition": "שְׂעֹרָה noun feminine barley ( bearded grain; ᵐ5 κριθή , ᵑ9 hordeum; Late Hebrew id. ; Sabean שערם Glas in Fell ZMG liv (1900), 256 , Arabic ; Old Aramaic שערה , ᵑ7 סְעָרְתָא , Syriac ; Di 260 compare Ethiopic wheat, grain ); — absolute ׳ שׂ Exod 9:31 +; usually plural שְׂעֹרִים Hos 3:2 +; — barley , common grain (often || חִטָּה , etc.): 1. growing, standing, singular Exod 9:31 (twice in verse) ( J ), Deut 8:8 ; Job 31:40 ; Job 1:11 , as sown Isa 28:25 standing, plural 2Sam 14:30 ׳ שְׂעוֺ 1Chr 11:13 , reaped קְצִיר (הַ)שְׂעֹרִים 2Sam 21:9 ; Ruth 1:22 ; Ruth 2:23 , ׳ גֹּרֶן הַשּׂ Ruth 3:2 . 2. plural, the grains, measured, cooked , etc.: Hos 3:2 (twice in verse); Ezek 4:9 ; Ezek 13:19 ; Ezek 45:13 ; 2Kgs 7:1 ; 2Kgs 7:16 ; 2Kgs 7:18 ; Jer 41:8 ; 2Chr 2:9 ; 2Chr 2:14 ; 2Chr 27:5 ; 2Chr 3:15 ; 2Chr 3:17 ; 2Chr 2:28 ; 1Kgs 5:8 (food for horses); ׳ זֶרַע חֹמֶר שׂ Lev 27:16 ( P ); ׳ קֶמַח שׂ Num 5:15 , ׳ לֶחֶם שׂ Judg 7:13 ; 2Kgs 4:42 , ׳ עֻגַת שׂ Ezek 4:12 .", "definition_html": "<h1><entry onclick=\"bdbid('BDB8287')\">BDB8287</entry> [<entry onclick=\"sn('H8184')\">H8184</entry>]</h1><div class=\"navigation\"><entry onclick=\"bdbid('BDB8286')\">BDB8286</entry> | BIBLICAL HEBREW | <entry onclick=\"bdbid('BDB8288')\">BDB8288</entry></div><p> <bdbheb>שְׂעֹרָה</bdbheb> <b>noun feminine</b> <highlightword>barley</highlightword> (<highlight>bearded</highlight> grain; <lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('Sept')\"><bdbheb><reflink>ᵐ5</reflink></bdbheb></lookup> <grk>κριθή</grk>, <lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('Vg')\"><bdbheb><reflink>ᵑ9</reflink></bdbheb></lookup> hordeum; Late Hebrew <highlight>id.</highlight>; Sabean <bdbheb>שערם</bdbheb> <lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('Gl')\">Glas</lookup> in Fell<sup>ZMG liv (1900), 256</sup>, Arabic <placeholder5304/>; Old Aramaic <bdbarc>שערה</bdbarc>, <lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('Tg')\"><bdbheb><reflink>ᵑ7</r